<% character = roll.player.character %><% used = character.items.used_since(roll.scene.created_at) %>In scene <%= roll.scene.position %> of <%= roll.scene.game_session.scene_budget %>, <%= roll.scene.part_of_the_story %>, <%= roll.player.name %> chose "<%= roll.choice.label %>": die <%= roll.value %>, modifier <%= format("%+d", roll.modifier) %>, statuses <%= format("%+d", roll.status_modifier) %>, total <%= roll.total %> against <%= roll.target %>. <%= roll.grade_label %>, margin <%= format("%+d", roll.margin) %>.<% if roll.grade == :narrow %> It works, but not for free: it costs <%= roll.player.name %> something on the way.<% end %><% unless roll.scene.last? %><% if roll.success? %> It hands <%= roll.player.name %> a clue from the plan not found yet, if one is left<% else %> It does not work, and that costs something within the plan: time, someone's trust or health. The story still moves on, not in a new direction and not back for a second try: if a clue is left, <%= roll.player.name %> comes by it anyway, late or at that cost<% end %> (<% if (found = roll.scene.game_session.clues_found).any? %>found so far: <%= found.to_sentence %><% else %>none found so far<% end %>). Show the clue plainly and add "clue": its number to the block.<% end %>
<% if used.any? %>Used since the scene began, already applied: <%= used.map { |item| "#{item.name} (#{format("%+d", item.hp_effect)} health)" }.join(", ") %>.
<% end %><%= roll.player.name %> now: <%= character.sheet %>.
<% if (companions = roll.scene.companions).any? %>In the scene with <%= roll.player.name %>: <%= companions.map { it.character.portrait }.join("; ") %>.
<% end %><% game = roll.scene.game_session %><% if roll.scene.last? %><% earlier = game.rolls.where.not(id: roll) %>This is the last roll, and the story ends with it: <%= earlier.where(success: true).count %> of the <%= earlier.count %> rolls before it succeeded. Victory or defeat is the story's to decide: weigh what the heroes found and did, this roll included, against the plan's endings, and give the ending they have earned. Tell what this roll does, then how the story ends, with only what the story has shown: what the heroes never found stays unsaid, and no one explains it. A roll that succeeds here gets the heroes what they reached for; a defeat comes from what they failed to find or do, plainly. The ending is only what the choices and rolls bring about: no one, <%= game.party.map(&:name).to_sentence %> included, makes a move in it that those did not set up.<% if game.party.many? %> Each of them has a part in it: <%= game.party.reject(&:departed?).map { |player| "#{player.name} tried #{player.attempts.to_sentence.presence || "nothing"}" }.join("; ") %>.<% end %> The block adds "outcome": "victory" or "defeat".
<% elsif roll.life_at_stake? %>This roll can take the last of <%= roll.player.name %>'s health. If it does, <%= roll.player.name %> falls and the story ends here in defeat: tell how, and add "outcome": "defeat" to the block. If not, tell only what this roll does, in a paragraph or two, and stop there: the next scene comes in my next message.
<% else %>Tell only what this roll does, in a paragraph or two, and stop there: the next scene comes in my next message.
<% end %>